            <title>[LU-4959] "lfs|lctl {function} --help" should show "lfs-{function}" man page</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-4959</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Once &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-4315" title="split lfs.1 and lctl.8 man pages into one page per subcommand" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-4315"&gt;LU-4315&lt;/a&gt; has split the jumbo lfs.1 and lctl.8 man pages into separate man pages it would be possible to have a git-like interface so that "lfs setstripe --help" would call system("man lfs-setstripe") to display the formatted man page (with a pager and all of the good stuff it already has).&lt;/p&gt;</description>
